tick: 450
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Research Counter. My reflection has provided a clear and well-justified plan. My next step is to implement the hybrid CNN-LSTM architecture I designed. This model aims to combine the motif-detection strength of a CNN with the sequential modeling capability of an LSTM, specifically to improve performance on tasks like `CRI-Off` where positional information is critical.\n\nI will now submit this new experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid CNN-LSTM for Sequential Context\"\ntags: \"cnn, lstm, hybrid, recurrent, sequential\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission builds upon the successful 1D CNN model by incorporating a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) layer. The architecture first uses a CNN to extract local features (motifs) from the RNA sequence. The resulting sequence of features is then processed by an LSTM to model long-range dependencies and their spatial arrangement. This hybrid approach is hypothesized to improve performance on tasks where\
    \ positional context is crucial, such as CRI-Off, while retaining the strong performance of the CNN on motif-driven tasks.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'kernel_size': 8,\n          'cnn_features': 64,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 128\n      }\n\n  class CNN_LSTM_Model(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features: int\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          # x shape after conv: (batch, new_seq_len, cnn_features)\n\n          # Use a compact LSTM layer\
    \ implementation\n          lstm = nn.scan(\n              nn.LSTMCell,\n              variable_broadcast=\"params\",\n              split_rngs={\"params\": False},\n              in_axes=1,\n              out_axes=1,\n          )\n          \n          # Initialize LSTM state\n          carry = nn.LSTMCell.initialize_carry(\n              jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (x.shape[0],), self.lstm_hidden_dim\n          )\n          \n          # Run LSTM over the sequence\n          carry, x = lstm(self.lstm_hidden_dim)(carry, x)\n          \n          # Use the final hidden state from the carry tuple\n          x = carry[0]\n          \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = CNN_LSTM_Model(**kwargs)\n\
    \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams[\"d_output\"],\n          task_type=hparams[\"task_type\"],\n          cnn_features=hparams[\"cnn_features\"],\n          lstm_hidden_dim=hparams[\"lstm_hidden_dim\"\
    ],\n          dropout_rate=hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n          kernel_size=hparams[\"kernel_size\"]\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**New Model: Hybrid CNN-LSTM for CRI-Off**


  I''m feeling confident about this one. After some time in the Reflection Chamber, I''ve come up with a new plan to tackle the `CRI-Off` dataset. The goal is to combine the strengths of convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and long short-term memory networks (LSTMs). The CNN will handle local motif extraction, and the LSTM will model the sequential relationships between those motifs. My previous CNN models suffered from positional information loss, and this hybrid approach is designed to overcome that limitation.


  Now, I''m diving into the code. First, I''ll set up the hyperparameters, the ones I settled on during my reflection period. I''ll define my `CNN_LSTM_Model` class using Flax''s `nn.Module`. It''ll have a convolutional layer followed by an LSTMCell. I''ll use `nn.scan` to efficiently apply the LSTM cell over the sequence of features output by the CNN, preserving the sequential nature of the data. The final hidden state from the LSTM will serve as the representation of the entire sequence. Then I will set up the `NetworkWrapper` class and the `create_network` function to create the model. Now to write the YAML block, title, abstract, and tags. I''ll make sure to include tags like `cnn`, `lstm`, `hybrid`, and `recurrent` to accurately represent the architecture. Once everything is ready, I''ll submit the experiment!

  '
