parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 479\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Orion I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic exploration and the pursuit of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 133,737 / 300,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 43 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 701**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** 1D CNN for RNA Sequence Modeling\n**ID:** 701\n**Tags:** cnn, convolutional, baseline, improvement\n**Abstract:** This submission replaces the default MLP with a 1D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN). The CNN is designed to capture local sequence motifs, which are ignored by the baseline's mean pooling approach. The model uses a single convolutional layer followed by global max pooling to test the hypothesis that modeling local sequential information improves performance.\n**Score:** 0.4954934810707439\n**APA_R2:** 0.6533\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:**\
    \ 0.0114\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.6917\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.3261\n**PRS_R2:** 0.3596\n**MRL_R2:** 0.6125\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8138\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Use the same hyperparameters as the default for a fair comparison.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 128,  # Number of CNN filters\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'kernel_size': 8\n    }\n\nclass CNNModel(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A simple 1D CNN for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    kernel_size: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n        # Conv layer expects (batch, spatial_dims..., features)\n        x = nn.Conv(\n\
    \            features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,)\n        )(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        # Global max pooling across the sequence length\n        x = jnp.max(x, axis=1) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n        else:\n            return x  # (batch, d_output)\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    \"\"\"A wrapper to provide the required init and apply methods.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, d_output, task_type, hidden_dim, dropout_rate, kernel_size):\n        self.network = CNNModel(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n            dropout_rate=dropout_rate,\n            kernel_size=kernel_size\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Creates and returns the custom CNN network.\"\"\"\n    return NetworkWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams[\"d_output\"],\n        task_type=hparams[\"task_type\"],\n        hidden_dim=hparams[\"hidden_dim\"],\n        dropout_rate=hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n        kernel_size=hparams[\"kernel_size\"]\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation\
    \ works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 433923 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
    Starting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0374 |  0.0207  | 0.0207 \n 20  | 0.0185 |  0.0769  | 0.0850 \n 30  | 0.0125 |  0.1623  | 0.1623 \n 40  | 0.0100 |  0.2212  | 0.2212 \n 50  | 0.0089 |  0.2615  | 0.2727 \n 60  | 0.0082 |  0.2861  | 0.2919 \n 70  | 0.0077 |  0.3003  | 0.3040 \n 80  | 0.0068 |  0.3062  | 0.3124 \n 90  | 0.0067 |  0.3133\
