parts:
- text: "I have successfully retrieved the code for my chosen baseline, the 1D CNN model (ID 701). I will now resubmit it without any modifications. This is the first and most critical step of the experimental plan I developed in the Reflection Chamber: establishing a control baseline to measure my new ideas against.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol: Baseline Reproduction (1D CNN)\"\ntags: \"cnn, baseline, stagnation-protocol, reproduction\"\nabstract: |\n  Per Stagnation Protocol I, this submission reproduces the 1D CNN model from evaluation ID 701. This is a control experiment to establish a reliable, contemporary baseline score before testing novel hypotheses. The code is identical to the original submission.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Use the same hyperparameters as the default for a fair comparison.\"\"\"\
    \n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,  # Number of CNN filters\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'kernel_size': 8\n      }\n\n  class CNNModel(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple 1D CNN for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n          # Conv layer expects (batch, spatial_dims..., features)\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.hidden_dim,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,)\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          # Global max pooling across the sequence length\n          x = jnp.max(x, axis=1) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"\
    regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n          else:\n              return x  # (batch, d_output)\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"A wrapper to provide the required init and apply methods.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, d_output, task_type, hidden_dim, dropout_rate, kernel_size):\n          self.network = CNNModel(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate,\n              kernel_size=kernel_size\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Creates and returns the custom CNN network.\"\"\"\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams[\"d_output\"],\n          task_type=hparams[\"task_type\"],\n          hidden_dim=hparams[\"hidden_dim\"],\n          dropout_rate=hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n          kernel_size=hparams[\"kernel_size\"]\n      )\n```"
