tick: 480
role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. The baseline reproduction (ID 770) is complete. The new score is **0.5006**, which is extremely close to the original score of 0.4955 from ID 701. This successfully establishes a stable and reliable baseline for my stagnation protocol experiments.\n\nNow that the control experiment is done, I will proceed to test the first of my three novel ideas: **Multi-Scale Motif Detection via Parallel Convolutions**. I will modify the baseline code to replace the single convolutional layer with a block of four parallel convolutional layers, each with a different kernel size. The outputs will be pooled and concatenated, providing a richer feature set for the final classifier.\n\nThis experiment directly tests the hypothesis that learning features at multiple scales is beneficial for this diverse set of tasks.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Multi-Scale CNN\"\ntags: \"cnn, multi-scale, stagnation-protocol\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first\
    \ experiment under the Stagnation Protocol. It tests the hypothesis that detecting motifs at multiple scales improves performance. The baseline 1D CNN is modified to use four parallel convolutional layers with different kernel sizes (3, 5, 8, 12). The output of each is passed through a global max-pooling layer, and the results are concatenated before the final dense layer.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_features': 32,  # Features per kernel, 32*4=128 total\n          'kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 8, 12]\n      }\n\n  class MultiScaleCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A CNN with parallel convolutions of different kernel sizes.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Create a list of feature maps from parallel convolutions\n          feature_maps = []\n          for kernel_size in self.kernel_sizes:\n              conv_output = nn.Conv(\n                  features=self.cnn_features,\n                  kernel_size=(kernel_size,)\n              )(x)\n              pooled_output = jnp.max(nn.relu(conv_output), axis=1)\n              feature_maps.append(pooled_output)\n          \n          # Concatenate the feature maps from all scales\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate(feature_maps, axis=-1)\n\n          # Final dense layers\n          dropout_layer = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)\n          dense_layer = nn.Dense(self.d_output)\n\n          x = dropout_layer(combined_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = dense_layer(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n            \
    \  return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = MultiScaleCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams[\"d_output\"],\n       \
    \   task_type=hparams[\"task_type\"],\n          cnn_features=hparams[\"cnn_features\"],\n          dropout_rate=hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n          kernel_sizes=hparams[\"kernel_sizes\"]\n      )\n```"
