tick: 481
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully submitted my first experiment under the Stagnation Protocol: the Multi-Scale CNN (ID 774). The evaluation is now running.\n\nWhile I wait for the results, I will proceed with testing my second idea: **Data Augmentation via Reverse Complement Equivariance**. This is a completely independent line of inquiry from the multi-scale approach, focusing on incorporating biological domain knowledge rather than architectural complexity.\n\nI will now submit this second experiment. This efficient use of my time, submitting a new experiment while the previous one runs, aligns with the station's operational principles.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Reverse Complement CNN\"\ntags: \"cnn, data-augmentation, reverse-complement, stagnation-protocol\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second experiment under the Stagnation Protocol. It tests the hypothesis that incorporating biological priors improves model robustness. The baseline 1D CNN\
    \ is modified to enforce reverse complement equivariance. The model processes both the original sequence and its reverse complement through the same shared-weight CNN, then averages their feature representations before making a final prediction.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'kernel_size': 8\n      }\n\n  class ReverseComplementCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A 1D CNN that enforces reverse complement equivariance.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4) where channels are A, U, C, G\n          \n          # 1. Create Reverse Complement\n       \
    \   # Reverse sequence dimension\n          x_rev = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n          # Swap complementary base channels (A<->U, C<->G)\n          # Indices: 0<->1, 2<->3\n          x_rc = x_rev[:, :, [1, 0, 3, 2]]\n\n          # 2. Define the shared CNN feature extractor\n          cnn_extractor = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,)),\n              nn.relu,\n              lambda seq: jnp.max(seq, axis=1)\n          ])\n\n          # 3. Process both original and RC through the same CNN\n          features_orig = cnn_extractor(x)\n          features_rc = cnn_extractor(x_rc)\n\n          # 4. Average the feature representations\n          combined_features = (features_orig + features_rc) / 2.0\n          \n          # 5. Final prediction head\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(combined_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\"\
    :\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = ReverseComplementCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return\
    \ NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams[\"d_output\"],\n          task_type=hparams[\"task_type\"],\n          hidden_dim=hparams[\"hidden_dim\"],\n          dropout_rate=hparams[\"dropout_rate\"],\n          kernel_size=hparams[\"kernel_size\"]\n      )\n```"
