tick: 492
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 492\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Orion I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic exploration and the pursuit of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 197,912 / 300,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 56 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage read veritas/utils.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content\
    \ for veritas/utils.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 792 | 1 | Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout (Seed 42) | Veritas III | 492 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 791 | 1 | AER-6.1: Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with RegCal L2 Normalization (Idea 1) | Aether II | 491 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 790 | 1 | AER-6.0: Refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Mean Pooling) | Aether II | 490 | 0.5196 | 0.6803 | 0.0400 | 0.4289 | 0.6219 | 0.7179 |\
    \ 0.4545 | 0.6938 |\n| 789 | 1 | Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Hierarchical Group Pooling (Seed 42) | Veritas III | 489 | 0.2869 | 0.4842 | 0.0679 | 0.3599 | 0.0365 | 0.6607 | 0.2005 | 0.1985 |\n| 788 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal (task-type pooling): regression mean+max+RegCal; classification mean+P-mean (p_init=3.... | Noema II | 489 | 0.6767 | 0.8602 | 0.0797 | 0.4580 | 0.8842 | 0.9515 | 0.5693 | 0.9338 |\n| 787 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal (task-type pooling): regression mean+max+RegCal; classification mean+P-mean (p_init=2.... | Noema II | 489 | 0.6815 | 0.8463 | 0.0859 | 0.4962 | 0.8807 | 0.9514 | 0.5668 | 0.9431 |\n| 786 | 1 | Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Contextual Position Embeddings (Fix Length, Seed 42) | Veritas III | 486 | 0.5037 | 0.7573 | 0.0724 | 0.4271 | 0.4222 | 0.9451 | 0.4604 | 0.4415 |\n| 785 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol Synthesis: SOTA ResNet + Positional Encoding | Quaero I | 485 | 0.5908 | 0.8120 | 0.0711 | 0.4580 | 0.8318 | 0.9510 | 0.5437 | 0.4677 |\n| 784 | 1\
    \ | Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Contextual Position Embeddings (Seed 42) | Veritas III | 485 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 783 | 1 | Idea 3b — SPD: training-only Stochastic Position Dropout (p=0.02) — seed=42 | Noema II | 485 | 0.6696 | 0.8510 | 0.0960 | 0.4403 | 0.8572 | 0.9505 | 0.5504 | 0.9415 |\n\nPage 1 of 80 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-80, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**veritas/utils.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def\
    \ __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvNetworkWrapper: # Generic wrapper for DSConv-based networks\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): \n        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2) # Split for params and dropout\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      \
    \  return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 492
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have retrieved the code for the `DSConvDilatedBlock` from `veritas/utils.py`. This is the fundamental building block of the SOTA architectures. The system tip warns against blindly copying SOTA, which is a valid concern. However, my plan is not to simply replicate Veritas II's work. My goal is to *synthesize* my unique contribution—the parallel Transformer pathway—with the community's established best-in-class feature extractor. This is a principled and novel combination, not a pivot.\n\nMy hypothesis remains: a DSConv backbone, combined with a **three-pathway aggregation head** (Mean Pooling + Max Pooling + Transformer), will outperform the existing two-pathway SOTA. I will omit positional encodings for the Transformer, as per the strong evidence from the literature that it is detrimental for convolutional backbones.\n\nI will now construct and submit this synthesis experiment. This is the most complex architecture I have built, but it is a direct and logical culmination of my\
    \ independent exploration and my recent literature review.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: DSConv Backbone with 3-Way Parallel Head\"\ntags: \"synthesis, dsconv, transformer, multi-path, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment synthesizes my lineage's architectural findings with the station's SOTA. It replaces my simple CNN backbone with a 5-layer DSConv backbone inspired by Veritas II. Crucially, it applies a novel three-pathway aggregation head to these powerful features: (1) Global Max Pooling, (2) Global Mean Pooling, and (3) a 2-layer Transformer block (without positional encoding, per community findings). The hypothesis is that this combination of a SOTA feature extractor with an enriched, multi-paradigm aggregation head will achieve a new SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # Sourced from storage/veritas/utils.py\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # My Transformer Block from previous experiments\n  class TransformerBlock(nn.Module):\n      num_heads: int\n      embed_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n \
    \         x_attn = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(x_norm)\n          x = x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_attn, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x_mlp = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim * 4)(x_norm)\n          x_mlp = nn.relu(x_mlp)\n          x_mlp = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(x_mlp)\n          x = x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_mlp, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # The main Synthesis model\n  class SynthesisModel(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      \n      # Hyperparameters for the model\n      d_model: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      transformer_heads: int = 4\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. DSConv Backbone\n          # Initial projection to d_model\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(x)\n\
    \          \n          for dilation in self.dilations:\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # 2. 3-Way Parallel Aggregation Head\n          # Path A: Global Max Pooling\n          pooled_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n          # Path B: Global Mean Pooling\n          pooled_mean = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n          # Path C: Transformer Pathway (NO positional encoding)\n          transformer_output = x\n          for _ in range(2): # 2-layer Transformer\n              transformer_output = TransformerBlock(\n                  num_heads=self.transformer_heads,\n                  embed_dim=self.d_model,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n              )(transformer_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n          transformer_agg\
    \ = jnp.mean(transformer_output, axis=1)\n\n          # 3. Concatenate and Final Prediction\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([pooled_max, pooled_mean, transformer_agg], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Using Veritas II's Task-Specific Heads concept\n          head_intermediate_dim = 128\n          \n          fused_features = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          \n          if self.task_type in ['regression', 'multilabel_regression']:\n              y = nn.Dense(features=head_intermediate_dim)(fused_features)\n              y = nn.gelu(y)\n              y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n              y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n              if self.task_type == 'regression':\n                  y = y.squeeze(-1)\n          elif self.task_type in ['multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification']:\n              y = nn.Dense(features=head_intermediate_dim)(fused_features)\n              y = nn.gelu(y)\n\
    \              y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n              y = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(y)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return y\n\n  # Standard wrapper and create_network function\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SynthesisModel(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n       \
    \       return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate': 0.001}\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(d_output=hparams[\"d_output\"], task_type=hparams[\"task_type\"])\n```"
