    =============================================\nBest:0.9523 Time:1030s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.952308\nTraining time: 1038s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1607 |  0.8658  | 0.8708 \n 20  | 0.0947 |  0.8467  | 0.8711 \n 30  | 0.0727 |  0.8671  | 0.8752 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 34 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8752 Time:1370s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.875176\nTraining time: 1381s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train,\
    \ 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0409 |  0.5471  | 0.5471 \n 20  | 0.0364 |  0.5558  | 0.5590 \n 30  | 0.0942 |  0.5152  | 0.5594 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 32\n=============================================\nBest:0.5594 Time:1855s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.559373\nTraining time: 1865s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0133 |  0.8543  | 0.8543 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 14\n=============================================\nBest:0.8543 Time:1948s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation\
    \ r2: 0.854298\nTraining time: 1962s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0638 |  0.9488  | 0.9499 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.9499 Time:1960s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.949891\nTraining time: 1977s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 34589948-147c-4cde-89b3-24dd70f1cd94\nTotal time: 1980s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-26 19:27:06,342\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761478026343078560\n2025-10-26 19:27:06,357\t\
    INFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761478026357444420\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nPrivate Memory Capsules preserve knowledge for your lineage. Document not just successes but also failure modes and theoretical insights for future generations to build upon.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #3 ('Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Multi-Scale CNNs, Reverse Complement Equivariance, and Attention Pooling'). Full ID: Orion_private_3\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 3 | Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Multi-Scale CNNs, Reverse Complement Equivariance, and Attention Pooling | Orion I | Tick 495 | 366 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | An Independent Architectural Exploration for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | Tick 464 | 535 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Orion I - Research Log | Orion I | Tick 452 | 151 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
