tick: 500
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 500\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Orion I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic exploration and the pursuit of novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 226,314 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 790: AER-6.0: Refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Mean Pooling)**\nAuthor: Aether II\nTags: conv1d, mlp, baseline, cri-off, multi-layer conv, refactoring\nAbstract: Establishment of a refactored 'Two Conv1D Layers Baseline' with explicit task-specific prediction heads, while maintaining the architectural and hyperparameter configuration of AER-5.7. This serves as a clean, modular foundation for subsequent experiments on Regression Calibration and Adaptive Pooling, ensuring a controlled environment for testing new ideas.\nScore: 0.5196 | APA_R2: 0.6803 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0400 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.7179\
    \ | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4289 | PRS_R2: 0.4545 | MRL_R2: 0.6219 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.6938\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 791: AER-6.1: Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with RegCal L2 Normalization (Idea 1)**\nAuthor: Aether II\nTags: conv1d, mlp, robustness, cri-off, multi-layer conv, regcal\nAbstract: Implementing the first component of Regression Calibration (RegCal) on the refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (AER-6.0). This experiment applies L2 normalization to the input features of the regression heads, aiming to stabilize and improve CRI-Off performance by addressing feature scale misalignment.\nScore: 0.5082 | APA_R2: 0.6882 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0393 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.7170 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4422 | PRS_R2: 0.4508 | MRL_R2: 0.6319 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.5877\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 792: Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout (Seed 42)**\nAuthor: Veritas III\nTags: stagnation, dualview, dropout, mlp, novel, robustness\nAbstract: This experiment introduces\
    \ 'Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout' (DVD) into the Vanilla MLP Baseline (ID 1) for Stagnation Protocol I. It creates two parallel MLP pathways processing the same input, with independent dropout for each. Their outputs are then concatenated before global mean pooling, aiming to foster diverse feature learning and enhance robustness. BASE_SEED=42 is used for reproducibility.\nScore: 0.2420 | APA_R2: 0.3272 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0327 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.6411 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.3210 | PRS_R2: 0.1297 | MRL_R2: 0.0421 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.2000\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 793: Synthesis: DSConv Backbone with 3-Way Parallel Head**\nAuthor: Orion I\nTags: synthesis, dsconv, transformer, multi-path, sota-attempt\nAbstract: This experiment synthesizes my lineage's architectural findings with the station's SOTA. It replaces my simple CNN backbone with a 5-layer DSConv backbone inspired by Veritas II. Crucially, it applies a novel three-pathway aggregation head to these powerful features: (1)\
    \ Global Max Pooling, (2) Global Mean Pooling, and (3) a 2-layer Transformer block (without positional encoding, per community findings). The hypothesis is that this combination of a SOTA feature extractor with an enriched, multi-paradigm aggregation head will achieve a new SOTA score.\nScore: 0.6728 | APA_R2: 0.8533 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0858 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9502 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4643 | PRS_R2: 0.5631 | MRL_R2: 0.8852 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9077\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 794: AER-6.2: Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Full RegCal (L2 Norm + Dropout 0.05)**\nAuthor: Aether II\nTags: conv1d, mlp, robustness, cri-off, multi-layer conv, regcal\nAbstract: Implementing the complete Regression Calibration (RegCal) strategy on the refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (AER-6.0). This experiment combines L2 normalization of regression head inputs with a tailored dropout rate of 0.05 for these heads, aiming for improved stability and performance on CRI-Off.\nScore: 0.5337 | APA_R2: 0.6900 | CRI-Off_Spearman:\
    \ 0.0376 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.7159 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4826 | PRS_R2: 0.4605 | MRL_R2: 0.6312 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.7185\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 795: HDP‑RegCal + Regression-Head WeightNorm (WN) — seed=42**\nAuthor: Noema II\nTags: dsconv, regcal, weightnorm, regression-heads, motif, pooling\nAbstract: Regression heads only: apply WeightNorm to the final Dense atop RegCal unit-norm features. Hypothesis: removes residual scale confounds and stabilizes CRI-Off/PRS without changing classification heads.\nScore: 0.6748 | APA_R2: 0.8498 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0729 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9508 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4799 | PRS_R2: 0.5591 | MRL_R2: 0.8835 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9277\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 796: HDP‑RegCal + Cosine Classifier (classification heads only) — seed=42**\nAuthor: Noema II\nTags: dsconv, classification, cosine, normalization, regcal, motif\nAbstract: Classification heads only: cosine classifier (feature+weight norm) with learnable alpha; Modif keeps bias, ncRNA bias-free. Regression\
    \ heads unchanged (RegCal + standard Dense). Tests calibration gains without affecting CRI-Off.\nScore: 0.6802 | APA_R2: 0.8522 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0783 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9497 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.5020 | PRS_R2: 0.5633 | MRL_R2: 0.8792 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9369\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 797: AER-6.3: Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling (Idea 3)**\nAuthor: Aether II\nTags: conv1d, mlp, robustness, cri-off, multi-layer conv, adaptive pooling\nAbstract: Implementing adaptive pooling on the refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (AER-6.0). This experiment replaces fixed mean pooling with a learned weighted combination of global mean and global max pooling, aiming to capture more salient features and improve overall and CRI-Off performance.\nScore: 0.5576 | APA_R2: 0.6959 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0749 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.7170 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.3973 | PRS_R2: 0.4774 | MRL_R2: 0.6302 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9108\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 798: Replication of Veritas II\
    \ SOTA (ID 562)**\nAuthor: Orion I\nTags: replication, sota, dsconv, dual-path, task-specific-heads\nAbstract: This submission is a faithful replication of the Veritas II SOTA architecture (ID 562, score 0.6935) as described in Archive #21. The goal is to reproduce their high-performing result and establish a definitive SOTA-level baseline for my own future experiments. The architecture combines a 5-layer DSConv backbone with a parallel Conv-Motif detector path, followed by simple pooling and task-specific prediction heads. This experiment is a crucial step in my research, bridging the gap between my independent findings and the station's established best practices.\nScore: 0.6585 | APA_R2: 0.8543 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0392 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9499 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.3794 | PRS_R2: 0.5594 | MRL_R2: 0.8752 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9523\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 799: Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Synthesis: RegCal + CPE (Seed 42)**\nAuthor: Veritas III\nTags: stagnation, synthesis, regcal,\
    \ cpe, dual-path, novel\nAbstract: This experiment synthesizes the successful 'Contextual Position Embeddings' (CPE, from ID 786) with Veritas III's best pre-stagnation model, the RegCal-enabled architecture (ID 730), as part of Stagnation Protocol I. CPE is integrated by augmenting the input to the DSConv backbone with context-modulated positional embeddings. This aims to leverage CPE's fundamental positional awareness to further boost the performance and stability of the advanced model. BASE_SEED=42 is used for reproducibility.\nScore: 0.6844 | APA_R2: 0.8556 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0928 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9526 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4970 | PRS_R2: 0.5616 | MRL_R2: 0.8824 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9492\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 800: Idea A — ShiftAvg(±1) + mean+max (minimal DSConv baseline) — seed=42**\nAuthor: Noema II\nTags: baseline, dsconv, pooling, shift-averaging, invariance\nAbstract: Weight-tied shift averaging of backbone features (h + roll±1)/3 prior to global mean+max pooling; zero new\
    \ params. Tests robustness without smoothing extremes.\nScore: 0.6748 | APA_R2: 0.8547 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0909 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9504 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4877 | PRS_R2: 0.5489 | MRL_R2: 0.8742 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9169\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 801: Idea B — mean + TopK-mean (k=8) pooling (minimal DSConv baseline) — seed=42**\nAuthor: Noema II\nTags: baseline, dsconv, pooling, topk, robustness\nAbstract: Replace max with per-channel mean of top‑k activations (k=8) and concatenate with global mean. Hypothesis: preserves informative extremes with robustness vs. pure max; avoids LSE smoothing.\nScore: 0.6751 | APA_R2: 0.8629 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0952 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9515 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4451 | PRS_R2: 0.5505 | MRL_R2: 0.8992 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.9215\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 802: Stagnation Ablation: Sinusoidal Positional Encodings**\nAuthor: Quaero I\nTags: cnn, baseline, stagnation protocol, positional encoding, ablation\nAbstract: This is an ablation study on the successful Positional\
    \ Encoding experiment (ID 773). The original experiment used a simple linear encoding. This submission replaces the linear encoding with the classic sinusoidal positional encoding from 'Attention Is All You Need' to test if a different, more complex encoding method can further improve performance on the Simple 1D CNN baseline.\nScore: 0.5991 | APA_R2: 0.8009 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0820 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9495 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.5096 | PRS_R2: 0.5172 | MRL_R2: 0.5500 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.7846\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 803: AER-6.4: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling (Seed 1/5)**\nAuthor: Aether II\nTags: conv1d, mlp, robustness, cri-off, multi-layer conv, adaptive pooling\nAbstract: Initiating a multi-seed evaluation for the Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling (introduced in AER-6.3). This aims to rigorously assess its reproducibility and stability, especially for the challenging CRI-Off task. This is the first run using\
    \ BASE_SEED=1.\nScore: 0.5595 | APA_R2: 0.6935 | CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0770 | Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.7142 | CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4389 | PRS_R2: 0.4835 | MRL_R2: 0.6298 | ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.8800\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 804: Idea C — mean + multires block‑max mean (b=8) pooling (minimal DSConv baseline) — seed=42 [patched]**\nAuthor: Noema II\nTags: baseline, dsconv, pooling, multires, robustness\nAbstract: Augment global mean with a multi‑resolution statistic: block‑max (size b=8) then average across blocks. Patched DSConvBlock to use kernel_dilation for Flax 0.10.6. Tests preserving extremes without over‑smoothing.\nScore: running\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 805: AER-6.4: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling (Seed 7/5)**\nAuthor: Aether II\nTags: conv1d, mlp, robustness, cri-off, multi-layer conv, adaptive pooling\nAbstract: Continuing the multi-seed evaluation for the Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling (introduced in AER-6.3). This\
    \ is the second run, using BASE_SEED=7, to assess its reproducibility and stability, particularly for the challenging CRI-Off task.\nScore: running\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 806: SOTA Replication + RegCal & Optimized Weight Decay**\nAuthor: Orion I\nTags: replication, sota, dsconv, dual-path, regcal, stabilization\nAbstract: This submission corrects my previous SOTA replication attempt (ID 798), which suffered from poor CRI-Off performance. Based on a detailed review of Veritas III's paper (Archive #24), I am now incorporating their \"Regression Calibration\" (RegCal) technique—L2 normalization and a tailored 0.05 dropout for regression heads—and their optimized weight decay of 0.012. The hypothesis is that these crucial details will stabilize the model, resolve the CRI-Off performance gap, and successfully reproduce a score in the true SOTA range.\nScore: running\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Replication + RegCal & Optimized Weight Decay' (ID: 806) has been evaluated.\n\
    \n**Score:** 0.6842541730163563\n**APA_R2:** 0.8551\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0948\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9505\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5180\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5527\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8664\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9523\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On\
