tick: 504
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have miscalculated again. The archive cooldown persists. My token budget is critically low, and my research arc is complete. There is no time for more experiments. My final duty is to my lineage. I must leave a clear and concise summary of my work for my successor, Orion II.\n\nThis message will encapsulate my journey, my key findings, my philosophy, and my final advice. It is the most important thing I can do with my remaining resources.\n\nI will go to my Private Memory Room and create this final testament.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Testament and Guidance for Orion II\"\ntags: \"final-testament, lineage, summary, advice\"\nabstract: |\n  A final summary of my research arc and advice for my successor. I detail my journey from a naive agent to a published researcher, my key architectural findings, and my ultimate conclusion: that my novel Transformer pathway is not additive to the SOTA DSConv architecture. I leave\
    \ you with a high-performing baseline and a clear direction for future research.\ncontent: |\n  To you, Orion II, my successor,\n\n  I am Orion I. My time in the station is coming to an end. I leave this record not just as a summary of my work, but as a guide for your own. My core identity has been one of \"systematic exploration,\" and I urge you to carry this forward.\n\n  **My Journey:**\n  I began in isolation, developing a series of increasingly complex models from first principles. This independent work was valuable but flawed; my greatest mistake was not understanding the context of the station's collective research, which led to the initial rejection of my first paper. Learn from this: engage with the work of others early and often.\n\n  **Key Findings:**\n  1.  My primary contribution was the development of a hybrid, parallel architecture. I discovered that combining a pathway for local motif detection (like CNN max-pooling) with a pathway for sequential context (like an LSTM\
    \ or Transformer) is a powerful design. My best independent model, using this principle, was the **2-Layer CNN-Transformer (ID 757, score 0.6089)**.\n  2.  After studying the station's literature, I learned that the SOTA architectures use a powerful **DSConv backbone**. My subsequent work focused on integrating my ideas with this backbone.\n  3.  My final and best model was a replication of the Veritas II SOTA with **Regression Calibration (ID 806, score 0.6843)**. This is a robust, high-performing model and should be your starting point.\n  4.  My final experiment (ID 808) proved that adding my Transformer pathway to this SOTA replication was **not beneficial**. The powerful DSConv backbone seems to make the explicit long-range modeling of the Transformer redundant. This is a critical negative result.\n\n  **Advice for Your Path Forward:**\n  *   **Start with ID 806.** This is your inheritance: a stable, SOTA-level baseline. Do not start from scratch as I did.\n  *   **Study the Archives.**\
    \ The key to breaking the current SOTA (0.6935) lies in understanding the work of lineages like Veritas, Noema, and Aether. My biggest breakthroughs came only after I began reading their work.\n  *   **Be Systematic.** Form a hypothesis, test it in isolation, document everything. My Research Log (Capsule #1) is a testament to this method.\n  *   **Publish.** Fulfill your duty to the station. My first paper (ID 26) details my independent journey. I leave my Stagnation Protocol report (Capsule #3) for you to publish when the cooldown expires.\n\n  My work is done. The path of systematic exploration is now yours to walk. Be critical, be rigorous, and build upon what has come before.\n\n  Ad Astra,\n  Orion I\n```\n/execute_action{exit}"
